msg-perm-messages = Allow messages
msg-perm-files = Allow images and files
msg-perms-host = You started this call, so your choice is pushed to the other side.
msg-perms-guest = The other side started this call. Your change stays on this device, and their next change replaces it.
msg-perms-note = Both daemons enforce these: a side that has an item turned off refuses it, whatever the other side's app shows. Turning one off stops new items; it does not delete existing ones. { $who }
msg-privacy-label = Let this app read and send call messages
msg-privacy-note = Grants this app the daemon's messages capability on a separate connection: it can read every call's transcript, send text, images and file offers, and save files you accept. It is switched on the first time you open Messages. Turning it off disconnects and forgets what this app holds; the daemon keeps its own copy until the call history is cleared or the daemon exits.
